  "name": "MYOGLOBIN SERUM",
  "code": "1161",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>Myoglobin is a cytoplasmic protein of cardiac and skeletal muscle and passes into circulation following damage to myocytes. Thus it plays and important role in Acute Myocardial Infarction, Early re-infarction and successful re-perfusion following theraphy. It is a very early indicator of Myocardial infraction, rising approximately 2 hours after the occurrence of symptoms. It reaches maximum concentration in the circulation 4 - 12 hours after the commencement of infraction and reaches normal levels in about 24 hours.</p>\n<p>As myoglobin is cleared by the kidney and change in GFR increases levels.</p>\n<p><strong>Clinical Use :</strong></p>\n<p>To exclude the diagnosis of Myocardial Infraction - If myoglobin concentrations remain unchanged on multiple early samples within 2 - 6&nbsp;hours after the onset of chest pain, there is an almost 100% certainty that cardiac muscle damage has not occurred.</p>",
